WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.801
-Jabari Banks, welcome.
-What's going on?

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:04.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:05.634
-Welcome to the show!
-Thank you for having me, man.

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:08.634
-We have so much to talk about,
including that your last name

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:10.734
is Banks and you're part of
the Banks family

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:12.133
and you're from Philly.

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:14.634
-It's a little weird.
-It's very, very weird.

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:16.234
But before
we even get that weird,

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:17.767
there's another weird thing
that I found out

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:19.234
that I want to know is true,

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:20.434
'Cause now you're the
Fresh Prince of Bel-Air.

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:21.434
-Yeah.

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:23.501
-But before that
iconic character,

00:00:23.501 --> 00:00:26.934
you were another iconic
character at Uni--

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:28.067
No, no. Where were you at?
Six Flags?

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:32.501
-IT was Six Flags, yeah.
I played Bugs Bunny.

00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:35.067
I dressed up as Bugs Bunny,
in costume.

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.534
-You had the --
-Yeah, the head, everything.

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:39.033
The eyeholes were, like,
this small.

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:40.400
Yeah, man, it was crazy.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.167
And, actually, I worked there
for only one day.

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:43.234
Quit the next day.

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:44.467
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:46.701
-So one day was enough.
-One day was enough, man.

00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:49.133
It was April,
and it was like 110 degrees

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:50.400
inside the costume.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.334
And we were doing, like,
the Cupid shuffle and the --

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:53.400
And everything.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.901
So I was like,
"Eh, it's not for me."

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:55.901
-"This is not" -- Yeah, you're
like, "This is not my gig."

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:56.934
-Unh-unh.

00:00:56.934 --> 00:00:58.501
And I actually spent
my whole paycheck

00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:01.434
on the snack bar at Six Flags.

00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:02.767
-That's very expensive,
the snack bar.

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:04.100
-It is.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.467
-But what made you go like,
"Maybe this is my job"?

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:07.767
"I'm a performer," or what?

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.234
-Well, I knew
I wanted to perform,

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:11.000
but I actually auditioned
to be, like,

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.901
a dancer in one of the shows
and I didn't make it.

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.334
-"You gotta start here, kid."
-Exactly.

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:17.067
-"You gotta be Bugs Bunny."
-I had to make my rounds.

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:19.200
Right.
-But now, look at you, man.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.400
You're crushing it.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.234
I mean, now you're cast as
one of the most --

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:23.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:25.601
-Thank you, thank you.

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:29.167
-Now, you're very young.

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:31.334
Do -- Were you alive when

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:32.934
"The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air"
aired?

00:01:32.934 --> 00:01:34.901
-No. No.
-Okay, alright.

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:37.834
-I wasn't even a thought.
-Okay, wow.

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:40.400
-Yeah, I think it
finished airing in '96.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.000
I was born in '98, so --

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.934
-Wow. So, did you know
anything about the show

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:46.234
or see reruns or --

00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:48.968
-My family -- we had
the six-season box set.

00:01:48.968 --> 00:01:50.968
And we had it in our house,
and so we would, like,

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:52.667
play it on rerun,
you know, all the time.

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:54.767
-Never thinking
you would be that.

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:56.200
-No way. No way.
-No. Not at all.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:59.200
This just went up recently
in the Philadelphia airport.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.601
This is a mural of you,
by the way.

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:04.434
-That is so sick, man.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:06.767
-I mean, what goes
through your mind?

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:10.234
What's your
connection to Philly?

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:11.767
-Man, it's crazy, like,
when I say, like,

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:13.000
this is -- It's strange.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.300
You know, like,
this whole experience

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.534
has been spiritual for me.

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.267
I actually used to live
with my uncle.

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:19.667
His name was Phil.

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:21.501
I promise you. I promise you.

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:22.667
Well, his name was James,

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:24.901
but we call him Phil
because he's from Philly.

00:02:24.901 --> 00:02:27.534
And I used to live with him
every summer,

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:29.133
and I went to school in Philly.

00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:30.501
-My brain is breaking in half.
-I know, right?

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:33.000
-Yeah. So, you used to
call him Uncle Phil.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.367
-Yeah.

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:36.367
-And you lived with him in
Philly or visited him in Philly.

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:37.367
-Yep.
-And your last name is Banks.

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:38.400
-Yeah.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.534
-And you're part of
the Banks family.

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:41.434
-Exactly.
-Wow.

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:42.534
-I played basketball.

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:44.167
You know,
I got the high-top fade.

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:45.501
-This is made for you.
-I know, right?

00:02:45.501 --> 00:02:46.501
-Yeah.
-It's fate.

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:49.000
-Are you also a rapper?
-I do.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.400
I was a rapper
before I was an actor.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.200
-You were?
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.801
-Did you go by Jabari Banks?

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:57.667
-No, I actually went by
Indie the Philosopher.

00:02:57.667 --> 00:03:00.400
I made it up.
It came to me in my dream.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.300
-Sure. Wow!
-Yeah.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.767
-Wow! Indie the Philosopher.

00:03:03.767 --> 00:03:05.033
-Yeah, It was probably
inspired by

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:06.133
Chance the Rapper
or something like that.

00:03:06.133 --> 00:03:07.300
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.400
And what type of rap?
What type of music?

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:10.567
What were you into?

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:13.033
-So, I used to listen to
"The College Dropout"

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:14.300
every night
before I went to sleep.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.434
-Kanye.
-Yeah, Kanye West.

00:03:15.434 --> 00:03:17.367
And me and my brother --
we shared the same room.

00:03:17.367 --> 00:03:20.167
-Is that the one where he had
the mascot outfit or is that --

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:21.367
-What'd you say?

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.734
-Didn't he have the --
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:24.100
The bear. Yeah, yeah.
The mascot.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.834
I thought you -- 'cause he does
another mask now.

00:03:25.834 --> 00:03:28.267
-Oh, a different -- I haven't
seen his face in three years.

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:30.167
Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:03:30.167 --> 00:03:33.267
But that might have been
why you were Bugs Bunny.

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:34.334
-Yeah, exactly.

00:03:34.334 --> 00:03:35.834
Oh! I didn't even put
2 and 2 together.

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:37.467
-You see what I'm saying?
-Full circle, man.

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:40.434
-Full circle.
Everything is crazy, yeah.

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:42.801
But let's talk about "Bel-Air."
-Yeah.

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:45.334
-It's a very different take on
"The fresh Prince"

00:03:45.334 --> 00:03:47.200
that we know --
or that we did know.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.534
But now --
Congrats on the great reviews.

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:52.834
How would you describe
this reboot or this new series?

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:54.667
-So, we called it a reimagining,
a remix, if you will.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:55.767
-Yeah, that's good.

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:57.868
-You know,
it's a dramatic retelling of

00:03:57.868 --> 00:03:59.267
"The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air,"

00:03:59.267 --> 00:04:01.567
and we get to take
all of these characters

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:03.734
that we know and love but peel
back the layers of them

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:06.634
and see, you know, what's
actually going on in their life.

00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:08.701
And, man, the stakes are high.
-Yeah, I know. It's good.

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:10.868
And Will Smith has been

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:12.534
super-supportive
of this, obviously.

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:14.367
This is his baby.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:16.934
-He's a really smart guy.
-Oh, yeah, he is. He is.

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:19.300
-He's unbelievable.
And we love him.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.567
He was our first guest
on this show.

00:04:20.567 --> 00:04:21.667
-Really?

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:22.667
-Yeah, when we did
"The Tonight Show,"

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:23.667
he was our first guest.

00:04:23.667 --> 00:04:24.934
Will Smith
sat right there, yeah.

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:25.968
-Really?
-Yes.

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:27.234
-In this chair?
-Right there.

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:29.033
-Oh, wow.
-Yeah, that's the real thing.

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:30.400
Yeah, yeah.
He'll let you sit there.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.334
-Okay. Right, right.

00:04:32.334 --> 00:04:34.501
-We'll call Will after the show
and make sure.

00:04:34.501 --> 00:04:36.968
-Right.
-Did he give you any advice?

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:38.767
-Yeah, man, a lot of advice over
these past six months.

00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:41.000
I mean, the biggest one that
I would say was, you know,

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.267
"Just be yourself."

00:04:42.267 --> 00:04:43.634
You know, 'cause that's all
he was doing when he was

00:04:43.634 --> 00:04:46.400
up there being the Fresh Prince,
you know, in the original,

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:47.534
you know, just being himself.

00:04:47.534 --> 00:04:49.334
And so I had to bring myself
to this role

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:51.067
and all my experiences
and my upbringing,

00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:53.567
and I feel that's what I did.

00:04:53.567 --> 00:04:57.400
-Do you do "The Carlton"
at all in this...

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.133
-I don't. No, no, no.
-No, you don't, no.

00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:00.701
-But you will see it
sprinkled in somewhere.

00:05:00.701 --> 00:05:02.300
-It will?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:03.868
-You will do it? Yeah.

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:05.968
Yeah, but you won't do it,
but Carlton will.

00:05:05.968 --> 00:05:07.801
-Oh, Carl-- Mm, maybe.
-Yeah. Maybe. Okay.

00:05:07.801 --> 00:05:09.100
-Yeah. Right.
-No spoilers.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.968
-Exactly, exactly.
-Yeah, no spoilers, yeah.

00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:12.501
-Do you do The Carlton?

00:05:12.501 --> 00:05:14.067
-I did --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:17.200
♪♪

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.067
-Come on,
you gotta give it to 'em.

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:20.734
You gotta give it to 'em.

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:25.634
♪♪

00:05:29.601 --> 00:05:31.834
-It feels good.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:31.834 --> 00:05:33.701
Here's Jabari Banks in
"Bel-Air."

00:05:33.701 --> 00:05:35.100
Take a look.

00:05:37.267 --> 00:05:38.601
-Know why I'm here from Philly?

00:05:38.601 --> 00:05:40.901
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:43.334
Little scrap on the ball court,
got nasty,

00:05:43.334 --> 00:05:47.067
now some bad man from Philly
want to deal with you.

00:05:52.033 --> 00:05:53.634
Rashad Denton, right?

00:05:56.534 --> 00:05:58.501
-Yeah.

00:05:58.501 --> 00:06:01.167
Yo, Rashad, man -- he's not
trying to squash this beef.

00:06:01.167 --> 00:06:02.300
He sent a shooter for Tray,
and now, apparently,

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:03.467
he knows I'm in Bel-Air,
so we've got to

00:06:03.467 --> 00:06:04.467
figure something out,
'cause I'm not trying --

00:06:04.467 --> 00:06:06.734
-Don't trouble yourself, will.

00:06:06.734 --> 00:06:08.801
I'll handle the situation.

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:11.701
-But how are you
going to handle it?

00:06:11.701 --> 00:06:13.200
-I said I'll handle him.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.501
No need to worry.

00:06:14.501 --> 00:06:16.133
No need to trouble
your aunt And uncle.

00:06:16.133 --> 00:06:19.067
I'll take it from here.

00:06:21.067 --> 00:06:23.634
-Come on! Jabari Banks.

00:06:23.634 --> 00:06:24.968
Jabari Banks, everybody.

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:27.467
Check out "Bel-Air,"
streaming now on Peacock.

